<title>GERMANY: Lufthansa to open call centre in Dublin.</title>
<headline>Lufthansa to open call centre in Dublin.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Lufthansa AG said on Thursday it would open on October 1 a new telephone reservation system in Dublin.</p>
<p>The German airline said the move was part of plans to expand its central reservations system in Kassel, Germany, amid plans to invest 4.9 million marks in the two centres.</p>
<p>Lufthansa said 45 new jobs would be created in the Irish capital for the project to handle overflow calls in Germany.</p>
<p>The airline said it considered sites in Germany but opted for Ireland due to cost issues.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
